## Overview
Learned about Blind XSS, where malicious payloads execute later in another user’s browser rather than immediately in the attacker’s session.

## Common Targets
- Support forms
- Feedback systems
- Admin panels
- Logging systems

## Example Payload
<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>

## Insight
Blind XSS is dangerous because it can target privileged users such as administrators without immediate visible feedback to the attacker.
